# Derived build of the community xLAM-2 8B port, with a context small enough
# that the whole model stays on the GPU.
#
# The upstream tag pins num_ctx to the model's full 131072 train context, and
# OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH does not override it. On a 12 GB Apple GPU that
# allocates an 8.7 GB KV cache, which leaves no room for the 5.3 GB of weights,
# so llama.cpp offloads only 24 of 33 layers and the rest run on CPU. Measured
# cost of that: 0.56 tok/s. Nothing about the model is being measured at that
# point, only the spill.
#
# 16384 is about 1.1 GB of KV at q8_0, so weights, cache and compute buffer all
# fit and every layer stays on the GPU. The longest observed eval prompt is
# ~1.5k tokens, so this clips nothing.
#
# Sampling params (temp, top_p) are inherited from the parent on purpose. The
# comparison measures the model as a user gets it, and the run-to-run variance
# those settings produce is the thing being measured.
#
#   ollama create xlam-8b-16k -f apps/api/src/eval/xlam-8b.Modelfile

FROM robbiemu/Salesforce_Llama-xLAM-2:8b-fc-r-q5_K_M

PARAMETER num_ctx 16384
